After ascending a wizard, I have really enjoyed playing healers. They
have a vigor despite early combat weaknesses, and starting with 20+ HP
gives each game a nice head start and a decent shot at the Minetown
Racket. I learned a lot of things the hard way after that, including
just how difficult the quest can be...

Anyway, in my last game once I got to Gehnnehom I had 204 HP, AC -22,
the Staff, +5 unicorn horn, a stack of +4 daggers, speed boots,
teleport control, 2 amulets of life saving and a bunch of wands; a nice
combination. This may not be "gospel," but rather than patiently
assemble a kit, I decided that I would just chase the &'s until the big
one came.

It was fantastic. I killed B no problem, J died like a grid bug, then I
got to Orcus and thwacked him with the rubber chicken and decided to
quit fooling around and get back to putting a game together.

But then I changed my mind and stone - to - fleshed Orcus back to life.
He promtly summoned Yeenoghu, both of whom slowly stalked me to the
upstairs. An uneventful battle ensueded, killing Orcus and leaving me
on B's level (no teleport) with Yeehaa left to kill.

That's when things started to cook. We were fighting back and forth in
the giant hallway and then Big D shows up. I finally get a good fight,
a fight which burns an AofLS right off the back from a deadly disease.
After this brush with death I promptly put my unicorn horn to work, and
with lots of fire and lightning E's I slowly crawled back to the
upstairs. The hardest part was getting through the non-teleport level,
several moments looked desparate, including an un-invited arch-Lich.
This guy actually helped me out, because surrounded by other monsters I
had a chance to fight with the staff and recover HP's without giving D
an opening. My plan was to get up the stairs, teleport to the next
upstairs, burn E and start hitting him.

Well, it took a three level chase to get this done, trading blows
between him and Y and getting a lot of good luck out of the unicorn
horn (my weapon of choice for this fight, not the best, I know.)
Finally, and unexpectedly, Y bit the dust and I am left with an
oppotunity to grab the <. With only two more fire charges left, I
secured the stairs and finally made some progress, wacking him with the
unicorn horn for 200 points of damage.

You killed Demogorgon.

Ah, the glory. Fabulous.


